# Root Cause Analysis

## Objective

Investigate every bug or failure to find the **true root cause** before changing code. Never apply speculative fixes.

## Diagnose Before Fixing

1. Observe the problem.
2. Gather evidence (logs, traces, tests, config, runtime behavior).
3. Identify the affected system.
4. Trace execution flow.
5. Determine the actual cause.
6. Only then implement the fix.

Never reverse this order.

## Evidence First

Base conclusions on observable evidence. Avoid assumptions.

## Reproduce

Reproduce the issue when practical. Understand the exact sequence that triggers failure.

## Fix the Cause, Not Symptoms

Remove the cause rather than hiding symptoms (retries without understanding, broad catch-all handlers, feature disables).

## Minimize Changes

Smallest reasonable change that fully resolves the issue. Align with project scope rules.

## Verify

Confirm the issue is resolved, no regressions, related functionality still works.

## Learn

Ask why the bug was possible; improve validation, tests, or architecture if warranted. Update documentation in `/docs` when the change is significant (see `documentation-first.mdc`).

